        "title": "Combine categories for one observation",
        "subtitle": "Turn a group of category numbers into one learned vector.",
        "disclosureTitle": "From category groups to learned vectors",
        "formula": "Select one table row for each category, then combine the selected rows for each observation.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A group belongs to one observation. Fixed rows have the same number of items; packed groups use boundaries, called offsets, to show where each group starts. Equal boundaries preserve empty groups.",
          "Mean averages selected vectors, Sum adds them, and Maximum keeps the largest value in each vector position. Real item weights work with Sum only.",
          "Whole-number categories and boundaries have no derivatives. A gradient describes how a small change affects the result; real item weights and trainable table rows can have gradients.",
          "Padding excludes a table row from the combination and its learning changes. Maximum norm limits selected row lengths, including frozen rows. Use CPU for maximum norm or trainable frequency scaling. Sparse gradients are unavailable with the current Adam training recipe."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open grouped-category classifier",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/EmbeddingBagWorkflowExample.swift"
      }
